    <summary type="html">&lt;p&gt;In just a few days’ time, U.S. President Donald Trump, Chinese leader Xi Jinping, and Russian President Vladimir Putin could be holding a three-way summit on the sidelines of next week’s Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation meeting in Shenzhen, China. According to The Wall Street Journal, Putin floated the idea of a trialogue last month as an opportunity to discuss ending the war in Ukraine.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.foreignaffairs.com/united-states/case-trump-xi-putin-summit&quot;&gt;Foreign Affairs&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;strong&gt;Tags:&lt;/strong&gt; #geopolitics #defense-strategy #number-theory&lt;/p&gt;</summary>
